From: jongkyung.woo <jkwoo@gooroom.kr>
Date: Sun, 26 Apr 2026 15:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Disable grub_lockdown() activation under custom GPG trust chain

gooroom-0008 disabled grub_shim_lock_verifier_setup() to prevent shim's
PE verifier from being registered when our linuxefi chain loads a raw
(non-PE) Linux kernel. However the surrounding grub_lockdown() call in
init.c was kept active.

Empirically, when SecureBoot variable is set to 1 in NVRAM (which OVMF
auto-sets after PK enrollment via efi-updatevar), the boot fails with:

    error: /vmlinuz-... has invalid signature.
    unaligned pointer 0x7bd9b509
    Aborted.

Tracing showed the fatal originates in kern/mm.c:139 get_header_from_pointer()
when grub_free() is invoked with a non-16-byte-aligned pointer. The path
that produces the bad pointer is reachable only when grub_lockdown() has
been called -- swapping NVRAM SecureBootEnable byte from 0x01 to 0x00
(which causes grub_efi_get_secureboot() to return DISABLED and skips both
grub_lockdown() and shim_lock setup) makes the same vmlinuz / sig / GRUB
binary boot cleanly through PGP verification, kernel start, and initramfs.

Since our trust chain is:
  - UEFI Secure Boot (firmware level) verifies grubx64.efi via enrolled db
  - GRUB PGP verifier (--pubkey gooroom-archive-keyring) verifies
    vmlinuz / initrd / grub.cfg.ima
  - IMA verifies userspace files

GRUB's internal lockdown mode adds no security to this chain (we do not
load arbitrary modules or use commands grub_lockdown gates). Disabling
grub_lockdown() activation removes the indirect path that triggers
grub_free() with a corrupt pointer while keeping all our verification.

Linux kernel still receives secure_boot=1 via grub_efi_get_secureboot()
in loader/i386/linux.c (kernel-side lockdown stays on as expected).
---
Index: gooroom-grub.git/grub-core/kern/efi/init.c
===================================================================
--- gooroom-grub.git.orig/grub-core/kern/efi/init.c
+++ gooroom-grub.git/grub-core/kern/efi/init.c
@@ -122,7 +122,8 @@ grub_efi_init (void)
    */
   if (grub_efi_get_secureboot () == GRUB_EFI_SECUREBOOT_MODE_ENABLED)
     {
-      grub_lockdown ();
+      // gooroom grub 0009: grub_lockdown() 비활성 — kern/mm.c:139 unaligned ptr grub_fatal 회피
+      // grub_lockdown ();
       // gooroom grub
       // grub_shim_lock_verifier_setup ();
     }
